From bb0b47ffe6e30d9d9ed4435d2e9c1b7b64d9f1fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: magnus_python <miguelsensacion@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 11:05:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AES-GCM: add constant-time software AES-GCM kernel
 (C/AesGcm.*)

Septima encryption expansion, patch 1/N: streaming AES-GCM
(NIST SP 800-38D) layered on the existing software AES kernel.

- C/AesGcm.{h,c}: SetKey / Start / UpdateAad / Encrypt / Decrypt /
  GetTag streaming API; in-place, arbitrary chunk sizes; 96-bit fast
  path plus general IV lengths; constant-time tag compare; state wipe.
- GHASH is BearSSL's ghash_ctmul64, (c) 2016 Thomas Pornin, MIT.
  Adapted only for 7-Zip types/endian macros; logic line-for-line
  identical, source verified byte-identical against canonical
  bearssl.org (sha256 a5a5986e621de057...).
- C/Aes.{h,c}: export single-block Aes_Enc_Block() (wraps the static
  Aes_Encode) for GCM keystream / GHASH-key derivation. No behavior
  change to existing coders.
- C/Util/AesGcmTest: cross-validation harness, 3036 vectors passing
  (36 edge + 3000 random: AES-128/192/256, IV lengths 8..128, AAD,
  ragged streaming chunking, round-trip, tamper rejection) against
  OpenSSL via python-cryptography.

Software-only fallback path by design; PCLMUL/AES-NI GCM fast path is
a follow-up patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
